  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norec, FK Norway, personnell exchange</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh, Burundi, Ghana, Kenya, Madagascar, Malawi, Nepal, Rwanda, Tanzania, Uganda, Zambia, Zimbabwe. The project, entitled the YESS Girls Movement (YESS - Youth Exchange South South) is a five year long programme. The first round will be virtual due to Covid-19, whilst the remaining four rounds will include physical exchange.   The project has two arm: the volunteer arm (for 18 - 25 year olds) and the professional arm (26 - 35 year old).

The volunteer arm of the exchange focuses on giving space to young women to develop leadership skills and play a meaningful role in identifying, speaking out and taking action on issues that affect them both on a national and a global level. This includes advocacy and awareness raising on e.g. gender based violence and menstrual hygiene.

In the professional arm of the project, participants will focus upon institutional capacity building of home and host organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
